{
  "version": "1.0",
  "initiativeCore": {
    "problemStatement": "Sales representatives consistently enter high-stakes calls underprepared — without a structured plan, without awareness of which discovery questions to prioritize, and without real-time support when conversations drift off track. Post-call feedback arrives too late and too subjectively to drive behavior change. Industry data shows reps forget 70% of training within a week, and fewer than 40% of calls follow any structured methodology (SPICED, MEDDPICC, etc.). Existing tools (Gong, Chorus, Clari) focus on post-call analytics and manager visibility — none provide decision support in the moment when it matters most.",
    "goals": [
      "Deliver an AI-driven pre-call planning system that reaches Minimum Viable Clarity (MVC) through LLM-powered conversational intake, replacing static checklists with adaptive questioning",
      "Provide real-time coaching cues during live calls — sparse, contextual, and non-intrusive (max 1 cue per 30-45 seconds) — surfaced at the exact moment they are useful",
      "Generate structured post-call deliverables: summary, scorecard (8 categories), one strength, one improvement area, and one concrete practice recommendation",
      "Support guidebook-driven coaching flows using SPICED (primary) and MEDDPICC (secondary) sales frameworks, with architecture ready for additional frameworks post-MVP",
      "Achieve sub-500ms latency for both coaching cue delivery and transcription display during live calls",
      "Prove the end-to-end loop — Prepare, Call, Coach, Review, Improve — in a single-user web application"
    ],
    "nonGoals": [
      "We are NOT building CRM integrations (Salesforce, HubSpot, GoHighLevel) in this phase",
      "No multi-user roles, manager dashboards, team reporting, or rep ranking — this is a single-rep private tool",
      "No mobile app — desktop browser only (Chrome primary, Firefox/Edge secondary)",
      "No PSTN/SIP telephony integration — audio captured from rep's local device",
      "No multi-language coaching — English only",
      "No emotion recognition, sentiment scoring, or engagement detection during calls",
      "No compliance enforcement engine or legal/procurement advice",
      "No persistent learning across users or longitudinal rep skill profiles (architecturally supported, deferred)",
      "No real-time scoring, probability boards, or advanced analytics during calls",
      "We will NOT build the full framework elimination decision tree — a placeholder (SPICED + MEDDPICC) is used for MVP, replaceable post-launch without interface changes"
    ],
    "businessImpact": "",
    "stakeholders": "- **Product Owner & Technical Lead:** Sole founder-developer — owns product vision, architecture, and all implementation\n- **Target User Persona:** Sales Representative (Individual Contributor) — runs their own calls, uses SalesCoach privately, wants to improve outcomes and consistency without manager oversight\n- **LLM Providers:** Cerebras (primary, fast inference) and OpenAI (fallback, broad model support)\n- **STT Provider:** AssemblyAI (v3 streaming API with turn-level formatting)\n- **TTS Providers:** ElevenLabs and FishAudio via Voice Engine proxy\n- **Design System:** Fuse Admin Template + Angular Material + TailwindCSS (Royal Blue #1D7AE6, Teal #0D7F86, Emerald #22C6B8)"
  },
  "requirements": {
    "functional": [
      {
        "id": "FR-01",
        "description": "Not extracted into functional requirements by the TPM contract (missing).",
        "priority": "must"
      }
    ],
    "nonFunctional": [
      {
        "id": "NFR-01",
        "description": "Not extracted into non-functional requirements by the TPM contract (missing).",
        "priority": "must"
      }
    ],
    "edgeCases": [
      "Not extracted into edge cases by the TPM contract (missing)."
    ]
  },
  "acceptanceCriteria": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-01",
        "description": "Pre-call conversational intake completes Q1-Q3 super-clarifying questions with LLM-driven data extraction and contextual follow-ups until all required fields are filled",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-02",
        "description": "Framework selection returns SPICED (primary) + MEDDPICC (secondary) and proceeds to guidebook-derived question packs for missing fields",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-03",
        "description": "Call Reasoning (CR1-CR5), Persona (P1-P5), and Demographics (D1-D5) stages complete sequentially, each gated by a fire-once completion event",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-04",
        "description": "Call plan is generated with: objective, 3 priorities, 2 risks, target next step, and unknowns list",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-05",
        "description": "Live transcription displays with speaker diarization (rep vs. prospect) at sub-500ms latency via AssemblyAI streaming",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-06",
        "description": "Coaching cues appear on-screen within 500ms of trigger detection, throttled to max 1 per 30 seconds",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-07",
        "description": "Post-call summary, scorecard, and lessons are generated within 10 seconds of call end",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-08",
        "description": "All extracted data carries confidence tags (confirmed, inferred, assumed)",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-09",
        "description": "WebSocket reconnects automatically (max 5 attempts, 3s delay) without losing call state",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-10",
        "description": "LLM provider failover switches between Cerebras and OpenAI transparently on provider failure",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-11",
        "description": "UI renders with OnPush change detection — no visible jank during live call with concurrent transcript + coaching cue updates",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-12",
        "description": "All event-driven communication flows through EventBus — no direct handler-to-handler calls",
        "testable": true,
        "priority": "P1"
      }
    ],
    "measurableOutcomes": []
  },
  "risksAndDependencies": {
    "internalDependencies": [],
    "externalDependencies": [
      {
        "name": "**AssemblyAI v3 Streaming API** — real-time transcription with `format_turns=true` and `ForceEndpoint` message support",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**Cerebras API** — primary LLM provider for fast inference (sub-second response for extraction and coaching)",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**OpenAI API** — fallback LLM provider when Cerebras is unavailable or degraded",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**Voice Engine Proxy** (prototypedemos.com) — proxies TTS requests to ElevenLabs/FishAudio",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**MongoDB** — persistent storage for users, campaigns, contacts, call sessions, transcripts, and call plans",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**SPICED + MEDDPICC Guidebook Data** — loaded from JSON into GuidebookStore at startup; defines dimensions, required fields, and question banks",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**Pre-Call Questions Schema** (`precall-questions-schema.json`) — defines initial questions, field metadata, and extraction rules for Q1-Q3",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**Fuse Admin Template** — Angular Material + TailwindCSS design system providing layout, navigation, and component library",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**Docker + Nginx** — containerized deployment with reverse proxy for WebSocket upgrade support",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      },
      {
        "name": "**AWS ECS** — production hosting (ECR for images, Secrets Manager for API keys, ALB for traffic",
        "type": "service",
        "risk": "medium"
      }
    ],
    "riskClassification": {
      "score": 21

{
  "assessment": {
    "1_do_guardrails_address_requirements": {
      "functional": {
        "status": "partial",
        "mappedAcceptanceCriteria": [
          {
            "acId": "AC-05",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "AssemblyAI v3 streaming API interface exists (supports turn-level formatting and ForceEndpoint), aligning with real-time transcription requirements."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-10",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "Cerebras and OpenAI interfaces both exist, which can support provider failover at the integration layer, but the failover orchestration behavior itself is not described in the guardrail summary."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-01",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "Cerebras/OpenAI interfaces exist to enable LLM-powered Q1-Q3 intake/extraction, but orchestration, stop conditions, and field-filling loop are not described."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-02",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "SPICED+MEDDPICC guidebook data and precall questions schema interfaces exist, aligning with framework selection + missing-field question packs."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-07",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "LLM interfaces exist to generate post-call deliverables; no guardrails described for timing (<10s) or queueing/parallelization strategy."
          }
        ],
        "missingFunctionalPiecesNotInGuardrailsSummary": [
          "EventBus-only handler communication (AC-12) is not evidenced in the guardrails summary.",
          "Fire-once completion gating per callId (AC-03) is not evidenced.",
          "WebSocket reconnect behavior with max attempts/3s delay without losing call state (AC-09) is not evidenced.",
          "Confidence tagging for extracted data (AC-08) is not evidenced (no data contract / schema described).",
          "Coaching cue trigger detection, throttling policy, and sub-500ms on-screen cue rendering (AC-06) are not evidenced beyond having LLM/STT/TTS interfaces."
        ]
      },
      "nonFunctional": {
        "status": "partial",
        "mappedAcceptanceCriteria": [
          {
            "acId": "AC-05",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "Use of AssemblyAI streaming API can support low-latency transcription; guardrails don’t explicitly address the <500ms end-to-end SLA."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-11",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "Angular/foundation tech mention exists (Fuse Admin Template), but OnPush/jank guarantees and change-detection strategy are not evidenced."
          },
          {
            "acId": "AC-06",
            "whatIsCoveredByGuardrails": "Cerebras interface exists for fast inference; guardrails don’t explicitly cover the <500ms cue SLA and throttling implementation."
          }
        ],
        "missingNonFunctionalPiecesNotInGuardrailsSummary": [
          "Enforced model name via env vars (constraint) is not evidenced; guardrails mention shared-lib interfaces only.",
          "Opus/Ogg browser streaming and decoder choice (constraint) is not evidenced in the guardrails summary.",
          "EventBus requirement (AC-12) is not evidenced."
        ]
      }
    },
    "2_gaps_and_misalignments": {
      "gaps": [
        "Auth method is TBD, while the contract contains no explicit auth requirements; still, the lack of decisions can block integration/testing and could become a hidden requirement.",
        "Data contracts/ADR are not generated (explicitly stated). This is material because AC-08 (confidence tags), AC-03 (fire-once gating), and AC-09 (call state preservation) require concrete schemas and behavioral contracts.",
        "No explicit guardrails for EventBus architecture (AC-12), which is a hard constraint in the contract.",
        "No explicit orchestration details for PCRC-LLM handler as sole orchestrator (constraint).",
        "No explicit handling strategy for WebSocket reconnect semantics (AC-09) and state retention.",
        "No explicit definition of LLM provider failover behavior (AC-10) beyond having both interfaces.",
        "No explicit latency measurement/validation plan embedded in guardrails for <500ms transcription/cues and 10s post-call generation (AC-05/AC-06/AC-07)."
      ],
      "misalignments": [
        "The contract requires: 'All backend handler communication must flow through the EventBus pub/sub system — no direct handler-to-handler calls permitted' and 'All event-driven communication flows through EventBus — no direct handler-to-handler calls' (AC-12). The architect summary lists interfaces only and provides no evidence that EventBus-only constraints are addressed."
      ]
    },
    "3_contradictions_with_acceptance_criteria": {
      "status": "noneFound",
      "notes": [
        "There are no direct contradictions stated in the architect summary (no claim that would violate ACs).",
        "However, several ACs are not demonstrably covered by the guardrails summary, which means we cannot verify compliance from the provided information."
      ]
    },
    "overallDecisionRationale": {
      "decision": "revision_needed",
      "why": [
        "Material acceptance criteria depend on behavioral/orchestration guarantees (EventBus-only, fire-once completion gating, reconnect without losing state, confidence tagging, throttling, latency) that are not evidenced in the guardrails summary.",
        "The architect explicitly did not generate ADRs/data contracts; given AC-08 and state/behavior requirements, this is a key gap."
      ]
    }
  }
}
{"decision":"revision_needed","concerns":["Architectural guardrails summary does not evidence compliance with AC-12 (EventBus-only handler communication) or AC-03 (fire-once completion gating).","Architectural guardrails summary does not evidence compliance with AC-09 (WebSocket reconnect without losing call state).","Architectural guardrails summary does not evidence compliance with AC-08 (confidence tags) or AC-06 (throttling + <500ms cue rendering).","ADRs and data contracts were not generated, limiting verification of required behavioral guarantees and schemas."],"summary":"Interfaces align with key external capabilities (STT/LLM/guidebook/schema/storage), but the guardrails summary does not demonstrate the orchestration, data contracts, and behavioral constraints required by multiple acceptance criteria (EventBus-only, fire-once gating, reconnect/state preservation, confidence tagging, cue throttling/latency). Material gaps exist; revision is needed."}

{
  "decision": "approved",
  "concerns": [],
  "summary": "Guardrails now materially address the contract and acceptance criteria: EventBus-only internal comms (ADR-001/AC-12), PCRC-LLM orchestration with exact-once stage completion guards (ADR-002/AC-03), confidence-tagged extraction loop (ADR-003/AC-01, AC-08), transparent Cerebras→OpenAI structured-output failover (ADR-004/AC-10), sub-500ms diarized transcript rendering (ADR-005/AC-05), coaching cue policy with render deadline/throttling/suppression (ADR-006/AC-06), WebSocket reconnect state restoration via MongoDB snapshots (ADR-007/AC-09), and post-call deliverables within 10 seconds (ADR-008/AC-07). No direct contradictions to acceptance criteria are indicated. Remaining notes (auth method and transcription confidence field mapping) are explicitly labeled as assumptions/TBD and do not contradict the contract; they are verification items rather than blockers based on the provided summary."
}
